# A list of whole numbers of which some pass 2 ** 31 holds doubles. Where the reader of an element wants an integer (`^`, `&`, `>>>`), the double was asked whether it is the integer that Link has said,
# then made a value (is it an int32? two roads, a join), then the value was asked what it is and taken apart again: 40 of the 48 instructions a byte of a checksum by table.
# The question of Link's word has truncated the double already: that integer is what the reader gets. The question itself is two stops, one for "no fraction" and one for the range, not two answers made booleans and joined.
# f1 = fold. past: the same read past the end of the list and at a hole gives `undefined`, which is 0 for `^`.
# -- source: a-double-out-of-a-list-goes-to-a-reader-of-integers-without-a-value-between.ts
